[Music]  so the united states says it's carried  out a drone strike against isil in  eastern afghanistan the attack in  nangarhar province follows an earlier  warning from president joe biden he said  his forces would hunt down those behind  thursday's suicide bombing outside kabul  airport at least 175 people were killed  including 13 u.s troops  well the u.s embassy in kabul is warning  americans against traveling to the  airport because of security concerns the  pentagon says specific credible threats  against the facility remain  officials say any americans who are  waiting at the airport should leave  immediately the united states and allied  forces are racing to evacuate their  citizens and vulnerable afghans before a  deadline to withdraw troops on tuesday  i will be speaking to charlotte bellas  about the situation in afghanistan in  just a moment but first gabriel elizondo  has more on the drone strike  uh the u.s central command  saying that a drone  attack  strike if you will  hit a isil  k  planner in the words of the u.s central  command  and that the strike was successful and  killed that person  they said this happened in eastern  afghanistan in the nangarhar province  that's province in the eastern part of  the country part of it borders pakistan  they say that there was no civilian  casualties that the u.s military knows  about now the reuters news agency here  in the united states  reporting that  information from unnamed u.s officials  that it was a drone that was uh launched  from a base in the middle east and that  it killed this isil  k planner who was driving a vehicle with  another associate and that both were  killed  we do not know exactly when this  operation took place  and we do also do not know if this is  one of more that are to be expected in  the future  but clearly the united states uh its  first retaliation uh for the attack  outside the kabul airport on thursday  all right let's speak now to charlotte  who's live for us in kabul and charlotte  understand you've just been up to the  airport and as the deadline draws near  i'm wondering who's in control there  yeah so last night we were told by some  taliban contacts that they were moving  more forces inside the airport perimeter  what they were calling their victorious  strike force units which are essentially  like their version of special forces and  that they've moved more of those  personnel inside the airport the us  denied that they had taken control of  the airport fully but we do understand  that they are slowly taking control of  more areas within the actual airport  perimeter and then this morning when we  went down we went to the north side of  the airport because in the last two  weeks that has been controlled by a  cia-run militia they're known as the  zero units and they're associated  obviously closely with the americans and  they had been separating western forces  from the taliban they had told us this  militia that they were going to be  evacuated by the us when this was all  done this morning we went down there  sure enough the taliban had taken  control of the northern perimeter they  said the handover began around 7 a.m  local time we could see pockets of these  zero units  surrounded by taliban and these these  two groups have been arch enemies for  some years now they've been surrounded  and the taliban was slowly taking  control of that stretch so certainly as  this winds down the taliban picking up  more areas of the airport  and what about the evacuations what's  happening there  well there were thousands of people down  there this morning still trying to get  on some of these flights we understand  that they are winding down when we were  down there we could see the tail of a  military aircraft near the tarmac if you  look at flight radar you can still see  c-17s entering and leaving afghan  airspace but fewer military aircraft  than there were in previous days and at  the moment they've evacuated more than  110 000 people whether they'll get uh  huge numbers out in the next couple of  days it doesn't seem so as as this  starts to wind to an end certainly us  allies have started to end their  evacuation efforts the turkish military  for example have said that their  military presence here has come to an  end but they for example are going to  leave a technical team behind to help  the taliban essentially run the airport  as of wednesday when all foreign forces  have left  all right charlotte leave there for the  moment thanks very much charlotte  ballister in kabul  so it's been called a life-altering  storm hurricane ida is making

